.TH GNL-God "" "12 June 2026"
.SH NAME
.BR GNL-God " -- get_next_line project tester (2026 Version)"
.SH SYNOPSYS
.RB bash " grademe.sh"
.RI [ "options ..." ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
GNL-God is a modern shell script that allows you to test your get_next_line project following the 2026 PDF standard.
It includes checks for Norminette, Forbidden functions, Compilation, and Memory Leaks (Valgrind).
.SH OPTIONS
Add successively all options you want, in the order you want.
.TP
.I "For example :"
.br
bash
.B grademe.sh -doom
.br
bash
.B grademe.sh -p2
.TP
.I "The following options are available :"
.br
.BR -h ", " --help
Display help and exit
.TP
.B -d
Allows to perform the tests even if the files are in directories
.TP
.B -c
Disable color
.TP
.B -s
Disable searching header file
.TP
.B -f
Disable checking forbidden functions
.TP
.B -n
Disable norminette
.TP
.B -u
Disable checking updates at launch
.TP
.B -doom
Enable Doom/Hardcore Mode (extreme stress tests, directory reads, multi-fd concurrency)
.TP
.B -p1
Disable Part 1 (Mandatory) tests
.TP
.B -p2
Disable Part 2 (Bonus) tests
.TP
.B -p3
Disable Part 3 (Doom Mode) tests
.TP
.B -op1
Do only Part 1 tests
.TP
.B -op2
Do only Part 2 tests
.TP
.B -op3
Do only Part 3 tests
.TP
.B ft_function-name
Test only this function
.SH FEATURES
.TP
.B Memory Leaks
If Valgrind is installed, the tester will automatically check for memory leaks in each test case.
.TP
.B Modern UI
Features a modern table display with box-drawing characters and progress tracking.
.SH BUG
For any bugs reporting, contact gemini-cli
